#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# d_fixed_points

#% text
# `d_fixed_points(eqs, vars, t)` gives the fixed points (equilibria) of the ordinary differential equations `eqs` in the unknowns `vars` of `t`: the constant solutions.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Each fixed point is a list of the state: for an unknown `y` of order `k`, the values of `y`, `y'`, ..., `y^(k - 1)` (the derivatives are 0).

#% item
# `vars` may be `y`, `y(t)` or a list of them; `eqs` an equation or a list.

#% item
# Solutions that depend on `t` are not constant and are left out.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
d_fixed_points(x'(t) == 2*x(t) + 1, x(t), t)
#% output
#= [[-1/2]]

#% cell
d_fixed_points(y'(t) == a*y(t) + 5, y, t)
#% output
#= [[-5/a]]

#% cell
d_fixed_points(x'(t) == x(t)^2 - 5*x(t) + 6, x, t)
#% output
#= [[2], [3]]

#% cell
d_fixed_points(y(x)^2 + 3*y'(x) + y''(x) == 2, y, x)
#% output
#= [[-2^(1/2), 0], [2^(1/2), 0]]

#% cell
d_fixed_points([x'(t) == -x(t) - y(t), y'(t) == 2*x(t) - y(t)], [x, y], t)
#% output
#= [[0, 0]]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `r_fixed_points`, `d_solve`, `solve`
